Modifications in this investigation include:
- independent plumb package/library/control/schema/access method and ~~> operator;
- planner binding isolation for Plumb scoring and highlighting;
- identity and public-Lead coexistence tests;
- scalar CTID postings with 256-page grouping and finite-set operations;
- experimental v1 postings codec, CRC32C, bounded decoding and corruption/allocation tests;
- default PostgreSQL page/WAL storage, immutable term segments, exact positive bitmap
  scans, online append maintenance, metadata inspection and database recovery tests;
- bounded batched bulk builds, wire-size-aware document admission, owner-authorized
  immutable segment merging and heap-first DDL lock ordering;
- development-dataset baseline tooling, CI changes and investigation documentation.

The inherited language crates retain their original authorship and version metadata.
Modified inherited Rust files additionally record dated modification notices.
The Plumb extension has its own 0.1.0 version and contributor metadata.

